{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01T9", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topology-section-space-jacobson}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:86ec2eecd570d0c8a4f479624baf284069e51967c1f2fc353abd21054aea9915", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4b5eb3b7eed6458aee8c19ba946e35e1af9f74ac6ef6326d88603647b4282bcd", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIt follows that most of the material from\nTopology, Section <REF_0001> goes through\nwith the set of closed points replaced by the set of points of\nfinite type.\nIn fact, if <MATH_0001> is Jacobson then we recover the closed points as\nthe finite type points.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1a99546581702d476862ea89ad3581949058cdd556d65c0d39c81f223434b3cc", "unit_id": "tag:01T9:prose-0004"}
